# Content pages are real paths (/help, /glossary, …) served by one SPA bundle,
# so every unknown path has to return index.html — with 200, not 301. A redirect
# would send a crawler back to / and undo the entire point of having paths.
#
# Netlify matches these top to bottom and stops at the first hit, so the asset
# directories are listed first: without them a mistyped /models/foo.glb would
# return the HTML page with a 200 and the loader would try to parse it as GLTF.
/assets/*   /assets/:splat   404
/models/*   /models/:splat   404
/fonts/*    /fonts/:splat    404
/hdri/*     /hdri/:splat     404

/*          /index.html      200
